@color(#FFFBAD) @info(compressed size of the header) @valid(!=0)
u64 header_size;
@info(compressed chunk data)
auto header_data header_size <<>> compression(lz4) {
    [
        @color(#7927F5) @info(points to the corresponding chunk) @valid(!=0)
        u32 pointer;
        @color(#6700FF) @info(size of the chunk) @valid(!=0)
        u32 uncomp_size;
    ]4096;
};


// ============================================================================
// .bitfmt SPECIFICATION CHEAT SHEET & ARCHITECTURE NOTES
// ============================================================================
//
// 1. DATA TYPES & BIT-STREAM ENGINE
//    - Types like 'u8', 'u64', or 'u12' mean "read X bits as an unsigned int".
//    - Unaligned bitfields (e.g. u1, u3, u4) read across byte boundaries
//      without padding.
//    - Arrays/strings of bytes use character array syntax: [u8 * length].
//    - 'auto' deduces its type dynamically from structural blocks or pipelines.
//
// 2. STATEMENT & STRUCT SCOPING
//    - Statements strictly end with a semicolon ';'.
//    - '[]' declares an anonymous scope (unnamed struct) that bubbles its fields
//      directly to the parent container via dot notation.
//    - '[ ... ]N' repeats the contained scope N times (array of structs).
//    - Array counts can be static constants (*4096) or references to earlier
//      parsed fields (*header_size).
//
// 3. PIPELINE OPERATOR (<<>>) - BI-DIRECTIONAL TRANSFORMATIONS
//    - Syntax: target param <<>> transform(algorithm) { body };
//    - '<<' denotes initialization/reading; '>>' denotes passing to a pipeline.
//    - Links reading & writing logic in one declarative binding:
//        * Deserialization: Read 'param' bytes -> Decompress LZ4 -> Parse body.
//        * Serialization:   Pack body -> Compress LZ4 -> Back-patch 'param' size.
//    - Implicitly aligns bitstream cursor to the next full byte before passing
//      buffers to byte-oriented transforms (LZ4/Zstd).
//
// 4. ANNOTATIONS & METADATA (@)
//    - Metadata attributes attach directly to field definitions for UI/validation.
//    - @info("description"): Provides hover tooltips and inspector documentation.
//    - @color(#HEX): Hues visual nodes and hex viewer bit-range highlights.
//    - @valid(op val): Dynamic assertion evaluated immediately upon field read.
//      * Implicitly binds field value as the left-hand operand (e.g. @valid(!=0)).
//      * Supports comma-separated AND conditions and dynamic cross-field checks.
//
// 5. EVALUATION MODEL
//    - Top-to-Bottom, Left-to-Right execution over a dynamic Symbol Table.
//    - Streams can temporarily freeze, spawn a virtual sub-stream (e.g. inside
//      decompressed blocks), and pop back to the parent stream once evaluated.
//
// 6. Structure
//    - Every .bitfmt file is a reusable format, meaning you can add a format
//      via an import and use it inside another (it will call format's code when
//      needed and will still be accessible via dot notation)
// ============================================================================